{"id": "EUVD-2026-106992", "enisaUuid": "749e9997-7e77-3352-9d21-22bf62884b63", "description": "FreeRDP before 3.32.1 on Windows contains a heap out-of-bounds read in client_cli_present_gateway_message that passes a byte count as wide-character printf precision. A malicious RD Gateway can send pre-authentication consent or service messages, causing the client to read twice the buffer size, leaking heap memory or crashing.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:36:21", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-c49c-xm94-5qf3", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-before-3.32.1-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-rd-gateway-consent-message"], "aliases": ["GHSA-36q6-xhpr-84hc", "CVE-2026-114041"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9dbd5f20-1c30-3dc6-b4cf-402814932439", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.32.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "83a1e03f-9fd7-38ae-9e1e-c5a892e82796", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}